---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Modernization for Government Contractors | Guiding Point Consulting"
  description="WBE/MBE-certified website audit and modernization for GovCon primes and nonprofits. Clear roadmaps, accessible builds, faster launches."
>
  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="service-hero container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Website Modernization</span>
      <h1>Website Audit & Modernization Roadmap</h1>
      <p class="service-intro">
        Your website is often the first thing a prime, a partner, or a program officer checks
        before they take you seriously. If it's slow, outdated, or hard to navigate, it's quietly
        costing you credibility — and opportunities — before a conversation even starts.
      </p>
      <p class="service-intro">
        Guiding Point Consulting delivers <strong>website modernization for government
        contractors and mission-driven nonprofits</strong>: a clear-eyed audit of what's working,
        what isn't, and a practical roadmap to fix it — without a 40-slide deck standing between
        you and action.
      </p>
      <p class="service-intro">
        As a certified <strong>WBE/MBE subcontractor delivery partner</strong>, we know what
        primes, agencies, and boards expect from a professional web presence, and we build toward
        that standard from day one.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-group" style="justify-content: flex-start;">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get Your Website Audited</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What You Get -->
    <section class="service-section container">
      <h2>What You Get</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>A full technical and UX audit: performance, accessibility (Section 508 / WCAG awareness for public-facing GovCon work), mobile experience, and security posture</li>
        <li>A prioritized modernization roadmap in plain language — what to fix first, what can wait, and why</li>
        <li>Hands-on execution: from targeted performance fixes to full rebuilds, depending on what your site actually needs</li>
        <li>Clean, modern architecture built to scale as your organization grows — not another redesign you'll outgrow in two years</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Who This Is For -->
    <section class="service-section container">
      <h2>Who This Is For</h2>
      <div class="audience-grid">
        <div class="audience-card">
          <p><strong>Government prime contractors</strong> who need a subcontractor partner to modernize a client-facing or internal digital property without adding headcount</p>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-card">
          <p><strong>Nonprofits</strong> whose website no longer reflects the credibility of their mission or the trust of their donors and partners</p>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-card">
          <p>Organizations that got a generic quote from a web agency and want a partner who actually understands compliance, accessibility, and public-sector expectations</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-this-box">
        <p><strong>What this is not:</strong> This isn't a template swap or a coat of paint. It's a structural look at whether your site actually does its job — attracting the right people, building trust fast, and holding up under real scrutiny.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Outcome -->
    <section class="service-section container">
      <div class="outcome-box">
        <h2>The Outcome</h2>
        <p>A website that loads fast, reads clearly, meets accessibility expectations, and gives primes, partners, and donors a reason to trust you before they've spoken to you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="investment-box">
        <h3>Investment</h3>
        <p>Website Audit & Modernization projects typically range from $2,500–$18,000 depending on scope — from a focused audit-and-fix engagement to a full site rebuild. We'll scope it with you before any commitment.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="service-cta container">
      <h2>Ready for a Website That Works as Hard as You Do?</h2>
      <p>Let's talk through what your site needs and build a roadmap that actually gets used.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get Your Website Audited</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>